# 4️⃣ 🧠 MEMORY / RAM HIGH

Suppose:

```bash
free -h
```

shows:

```text
RAM = 16 GB
used = 15 GB
```

Don't immediately conclude:

> "Application memory leak hai."

First understand RAM + cache + swap.

Check:

```bash
free -h
```

Then:

```bash
top
```

Find which process consumes RAM:

```bash
ps aux --sort=-%mem | head
```

Example:

```text
java    12GB
mysql    2GB
nginx   200MB
```

Now Java is the main consumer.

---

# 5️⃣ Java Memory Troubleshooting

Java application mein important concept:

```text
OS RAM
   ↓
Java Process
   ↓
JVM
   ↓
Heap
   ↓
Objects
```

Check Java process:

```bash
ps aux --sort=-%mem | head
```

Check JVM configuration:

```bash
jcmd <PID> VM.flags
```

Heap information:

```bash
jcmd <PID> GC.heap_info
```

Heap dump:

```bash
jmap -dump:live,format=b,file=heap.hprof <PID>
```

Then analyze `heap.hprof` using tools such as Eclipse MAT.

---

# 6️⃣ Memory problem ke common reasons

Java/Spring Boot application mein:

```text
Memory High
    ↓
Too many objects
    ↓
Large collections
    ↓
Cache growing
    ↓
Memory leak
    ↓
Large heap
    ↓
Too many requests
```

Another important thing:

### JVM Heap ≠ Entire RAM

For example:

```text
Server RAM = 16 GB

JVM Heap = 8 GB
```

Doesn't mean Java can only consume 8 GB.

Java process can also use:

```text
Heap
+ Metaspace
+ Threads
+ Native memory
+ Direct buffers
+ JVM overhead
```

So:

```text
OS RAM
   ↓
Java process
   ├── Heap
   ├── Metaspace
   ├── Threads
   └── Native memory
```

