# 7️⃣ 🚨 SWAP

Check:

```bash
free -h
```

Example:

```text
Swap:
total 4G
used 3.5G
```

Heavy swap usage can make application **very slow** because disk is being used as memory.

Check:

```bash
swapon --show
```

You can also inspect:

```bash
vmstat 1
```

Important concept:

```text
RAM full
 ↓
Kernel may use SWAP
 ↓
Disk I/O increases
 ↓
Application becomes slow
```

So **high disk I/O can actually be a symptom of memory pressure.**

