# 8️⃣ 💾 DISK — But first ask: "Which disk problem?"

This is extremely important.

When someone says:

> "Disk problem hai."

There are actually **two different problems**:

```text
              DISK
                |
       ┌────────┴────────┐
       ↓                 ↓
  Disk SPACE          Disk I/O
       ↓                 ↓
  95% full          Slow read/write
```

---

# 9️⃣ Disk SPACE HIGH

First:

```bash
df -h
```

Example:

```text
/dev/sda1    100G    95G    5G    95% /
```

Now:

> Root filesystem is 95% full.

Next question:

> **What is consuming the space?**

```bash
du -sh /*
```

Better:

```bash
du -sh /var/*
```

Then:

```bash
du -sh /var/log/*
```

Maybe:

```text
/var/log = 60G
```

Now investigate logs.

---

# 🔟 Find large files

```bash
find / -type f -size +1G 2>/dev/null
```

Or:

```bash
du -ah /var | sort -rh | head
```

Common culprits:

```text
application logs
Docker images
Docker containers
old backups
temporary files
core dumps
large heap dumps
```

