# 1️⃣1️⃣ Java application + Disk

Very common production scenario:

```text
Spring Boot
    ↓
logs
    ↓
application.log
    ↓
10 GB
    ↓
Disk 100%
    ↓
Application problems
```

Check:

```bash
du -sh /var/log/*
```

Check application logs:

```bash
ls -lh
```

Use:

```bash
tail -f application.log
```

Search errors:

```bash
grep -i "error" application.log
```

or:

```bash
grep -i "exception" application.log
```

### Important

Don't randomly:

```bash
rm -rf /var/log/*
```

in production.

First understand **log rotation, retention and which process owns the file**.

