# 1️⃣4️⃣ Process Troubleshooting

These commands **must know**:

### List processes

```bash
ps aux
```

### Find Java

```bash
ps -ef | grep java
```

### CPU-wise

```bash
ps aux --sort=-%cpu | head
```

### Memory-wise

```bash
ps aux --sort=-%mem | head
```

### Process details

```bash
ps -p <PID> -f
```

### Kill

```bash
kill <PID>
```

Force kill only when appropriate:

```bash
kill -9 <PID>
```

### Why not directly kill -9?

Because graceful shutdown may not happen.

Preferred:

```text
kill
 ↓
application gets termination signal
 ↓
cleanup
 ↓
shutdown
```

