# 🔥 Kubernetes CPU/MEMORY troubleshooting

Suppose:

```text
Pod restarting
```

First:

```bash
kubectl get pods
```

You see:

```text
CrashLoopBackOff
```

Then:

```bash
kubectl describe pod <pod>
```

Look at:

```text
Events
Last State
Reason
Exit Code
```

Logs:

```bash
kubectl logs <pod> --previous
```

If:

```text
OOMKilled
```

then:

> Container exceeded its memory limit.

Check:

```yaml
resources:
  requests:
    memory: "512Mi"
  limits:
    memory: "1Gi"
```

Concept:

```text
Java Application
      ↓
Container
      ↓
Memory limit = 1 GB
      ↓
Application exceeds limit
      ↓
OOMKilled
```

